<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44201" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sigma</span></b> , ătis,
		n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σίγμα</span> (the Greek
		letter sigma; hence, from its more ancient form, C). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A semicircular couch</i> for reclining at meals,
				<i><span class="en">Mart. 10, 48, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">14, 87, 2</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Lampr. Heliog.
			25</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A bathing-tub</i> of the same shape,
					<i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 2, 2 <i>med.</i></span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Carm. 17,
			6</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
